<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 121 0 R/E(Thank you to everyone who joined us on Saturday, September 19 at Fairwood Park for the annual Lakewood Village Summer Picnic! It was a sunny, fun-filled afternoon bringing together longtime residents and new neighbors alike. There were about 75-90 attendees this year. From delicious tacos, fruit salad, refreshing frescas, desserts and sweets to outdoor lawn games, board games for the kids, Bingo games and prizes for all, the picnic showed once again what a warm, welcoming community we have here in Lakewood Village. )/Pg 11 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

157 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 121 0 R/E(A special thank you to all the volunteers who helped make the picnic a success! Shout out to Erika and some neighborhood kids and youth and friends for painting the canvas banners that we hung up at the entrances of Lakewood Village. Much appreciation to Bev for procuring 2 gift cards from Smoker Eaters, Jamba Juice and frozen donuts from Krispy Kreme. Our local partner, Walmart generously donated water bottles, plates, napkins, muffins and cupcakes. Thank you to Darryl and Jessie for coming early to help set up tables and put table cloths on the picnic tables. Thank you to Aarti, Nupur & Saurabh for signing in attendees with name tags and meal tickets. Erika facilitated the ice breaker questions and Bingo games with fun prizes! And last but not least to the helping hands of Bev & Robin, and Keith for cleaning up afterwards. Our neighborhood events wouldn't be possible without each neighbor showing up and engaging and participating\203your presence is what builds our community!!)/Pg 11 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

