219 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 125 0 R/T(Village Vistas: Autumn Splashes of Purple at the Playground)/E(Village Vistas: Autumn Splashes of Purple at the Playground)/Pg 15 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

220 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 125 0 R/E(Even as cooler mornings settle over Lakewood Village and trees begin their autumn turn, bursts of color are still thriving across the neighborhood. If you take a stroll past the playground under the bright orange shade sails, you will spot low, spreading mounds of lavender-purple blossoms brightening the mulch.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

221 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 125 0 R/E(These cheerful blooms belong to trailing lantana \(Lantana montevidensis\), a tough, drought-tolerant perennial that feels right at home in our sunny climate. While many summer favorites fade by mid-autumn, trailing lantana continues to bloom generously. Each delicate cluster features rings of tiny purple petals surrounding warm yellow-and-white centers, framed by textured, fragrant green leaves.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

222 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 125 0 R/E(It is easy to see why city landscapers and local gardeners love it. Trailing lantana shrugs off heat, needs very little water once established, and forms a dense, weed-suppressing carpet that stays green through most of the year. On warm autumn afternoons, the flowers double as a bustling stop for local honeybees and butterflies gathering late-season nectar.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

223 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 125 0 R/E(Next time you are out for a walk, heading over to the playground, or chatting with neighbors on the sidewalk, take a closer look at these resilient little blooms keeping our shared greenspaces colorful.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

